  "label": "Moral Equivalence Rhetoric",
  "description": "A rhetorical strategy used in political discourse to frame an issue as universally just or morally imperative, often by invoking personal identification or empathy. In this meme, the phrase 'you would want the same for yourself!' is a classic example, attempting to pressure the audience into aligning with a position by appealing to their own self-interest or moral compass.",
